        "    \n",
        "---"
      ],
      "id": "44e006c1"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "from lets_plot import *\n",
        "\n",
        "LetsPlot.setup_html(isolated_frame=True)"
      ],
      "id": "f69dac3a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Learn morea about Code Cells: https://quarto.org/docs/reference/cells/cells-jupyter.html\n",
        "\n",
        "# Include and execute your code here\n",
        "df = pd.read_json(\"https://github.com/byuidatascience/data4missing/raw/master/data-raw/flights_missing/flights_missing.json\")\n",
        "df"
      ],
      "id": "a6519456",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Elevator pitch\n",
        "_A SHORT (2-3 SENTENCES) PARAGRAPH THAT `DESCRIBES KEY INSIGHTS` TAKEN FROM METRICS IN THE PROJECT RESULTS THINK TOP OR MOST IMPORTANT RESULTS._ (Note: this is not a summary of the project, but a summary of the results.)\n",
        "\n",
        "_A Client has requested this analysis and this is your one shot of what you would say to your boss in a 2 min elevator ride before he takes your report and hands it to the client._\n",
        "\n",
        "## QUESTION|TASK 1\n",
        "\n",
        "__Fix all of the varied missing data types in the data to be consistent (all missing values should be displayed as “NaN”).__ In your report include one record example (one row) from your new data, in the raw JSON format. Your example should display the \"NaN\" for at least one missing value.__  \n",
        "\n",
        "_type your results and analysis here_\n"
      ],
      "id": "2fcc3664"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Include and execute your code here\n",
        "# Sort the dataframe based on the “month” column in ascending order and select the first 5 rows\n",
        "data = df.sort_values(\"month\", ascending=True).head(5)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Convert to JSON format\n",
        "json_data = data.to_json(orient=\"records\", indent=4)\n",
        "print(json_data)"
      ],
      "id": "d561d4d5",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## QUESTION|TASK 2\n",
        "\n",
        "__Which airport has the worst delays?__ Describe the metric you chose, and why you chose it to determine the “worst” airport. Your answer should include a summary table that lists (for each airport) the total number of flights, total number of delayed flights, proportion of delayed flights, and average delay time in hours.   \n",
        "\n",
        "_type your results and analysis here_\n"
      ],
      "id": "8f08473c"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Include and execute your code here\n",
        "# Group by airport and calculate required metrics\n",
        "airport_metrics = df.groupby(\"airport_code\").agg(\n",
        "    total_flights=(\"num_of_flights_total\", \"sum\"),\n",
        "    total_delayed_flights=(\"num_of_delays_total\", \"sum\"),\n",
        "    average_delay_time=(\"minutes_delayed_total\", lambda x: x.sum() / df[\"num_of_delays_total\"].sum() / 60)\n",
        ").reset_index()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Calculate the proportion of delayed flights\n",
        "airport_metrics[\"proportion_of_delayed_flights\"] = airport_metrics[\"total_delayed_flights\"] / airport_metrics[\"total_flights\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "# Sort the aggregated metrics\n",
        "airport_metrics = airport_metrics.sort_values(by=\"proportion_of_delayed_flights\", ascending=False)\n",
        "display(airport_metrics)\n"
      ],
      "id": "3f574358",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## QUESTION|TASK 3\n",
        "\n",
        "__What is the best month to fly if you want to avoid delays of any length?__ Describe the metric you chose and why you chose it to calculate your answer. Include one chart to help support your answer, with the x-axis ordered by month. (To answer this question, you will need to remove any rows that are missing the `Month` variable.)  \n",
        "\n",
        "_type your results and analysis here_\n"
      ],
      "id": "afdee7d3"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Include and execute your code here\n",
        "# Create new column for the month\n",
        "airport_metrics = df.groupby(\"month\").agg(\n",
        "    total_flights=(\"num_of_flights_total\", \"sum\"),\n",
        "    total_delayed_flights=(\"num_of_delays_total\", \"sum\")\n",
        ").assign(\n",
        "    delay_flight_month=lambda x: x.total_delayed_flights / x.total_flights\n",
        ").reset_index()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Remove rows with missing values in the month column\n",
        "airport_metrics = airport_metrics[airport_metrics.month != \"NaN\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "# Ensure the month column is ordered by month number\n",
        "airport_metrics[\"month\"] = pd.Categorical(\n",
        "    airport_metrics[\"month\"],\n",
        "    categories=[\n",
        "        \"January\", \"February\", \"March\", \"April\", \"May\", \"June\",\n",
        "        \"July\", \"August\", \"September\", \"October\", \"November\", \"December\"\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    ordered=True\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Sort the dataframe by month\n",
        "airport_metrics = airport_metrics.sort_values(\"month\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Plot using Plotly Express\n",
        "import plotly.express as px\n",
        "fig = px.bar(\n",
        "    airport_metrics, x=\"month\", y=\"delay_flight_month\",\n",
        "    labels={\"month\": \"Month\", \"delay_flight_month\": \"Average Delay Flights\"}\n",
        ")\n",
        "fig.show()"
      ],
      "id": "c300e696",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## QUESTION|TASK 4\n",
        "\n",
        "According to the BTS website, the “Weather” category only accounts for severe weather delays. Mild weather delays are not counted in the “Weather” category, but are actually included in both the “NAS” and “Late-Arriving Aircraft” categories. __Your job is to create a new column that calculates the total number of flights delayed by weather (both severe and mild).__ You will need to replace all the missing values in the Late Aircraft variable with the mean. Show your work by printing the first 5 rows of data in a table. Use these three rules for your calculations:  \n",
        "\n",
        "    a. 100% of delayed flights in the Weather category are due to weather  \n",
        "    b. 30% of all delayed flights in the Late-Arriving category are due to weather  \n",
        "    c. From April to August, 40% of delayed flights in the NAS category are due to weather. The rest of the months, the proportion rises to 65%    \n",
        "\n",
        "_type your results and analysis here_\n"
      ],
      "id": "3eb62542"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Include and execute your code here\n",
        "# Calculate total_weather_delays (Task 4)\n",
        "def calculate_total_weather_delays(row):\n",
        "    weather = row.get(\"num_of_delays_weather\", 0) or 0\n",
        "    late = row.get(\"num_of_delays_late_aircraft\", 0) or 0\n",
        "    nas = row.get(\"num_of_delays_nas\", 0) or 0\n",
        "    month = row.get(\"month\", \"\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    weather_part = weather\n",
        "    late_part = late * 0.3\n",
        "\n",
        "    months_apr_to_aug = [\"April\", \"May\", \"June\", \"July\", \"August\"]\n",
        "    nas_factor = 0.4 if month in months_apr_to_aug else 0.65\n",
        "    nas_part = nas * nas_factor\n",
        "\n",
        "    return round(weather_part + late_part + nas_part, 2)\n",
        "\n",
        "df[\"total_weather_delays\"] = df.apply(calculate_total_weather_delays, axis=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Part A: only delays from the Weather category\n",
        "\n",
        "# Load and prepare data\n",
        "url_flights = 'https://github.com/byuidatascience/data4missing/raw/master/data-raw/flights_missing/flights_missing.json'\n",
        "df = pd.read_json(url_flights)\n",
        "df.replace([-999, \"1500+\", \"n/a\", \"\", None, 'NaN'], np.nan, inplace=True)\n",
        "df[\"num_of_delays_weather\"] = df[\"num_of_delays_weather\"].astype(float)\n",
        "\n",
        "# calculate total weather delays (only from the Weather category)\n",
        "df[\"total_weather_delays_A\"] = df[\"num_of_delays_weather\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "# Visualization\n",
        "display(df[[\"airport_code\", \"month\", \"num_of_delays_weather\", \"total_weather_delays_A\"]].head())"
      ],
      "id": "def8e047",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Include and execute your code here\n",
        "# Part B: 30% of the delays in the Late-Arriving Aircraft category are due to weather\n",
        "\n",
        "# Replace missing values and convert to float\n",
        "df[\"num_of_delays_late_aircraft\"] = df[\"num_of_delays_late_aircraft\"].replace(\"NaN\", np.nan).astype(float)\n",
        "late_aircraft_mean = df[\"num_of_delays_late_aircraft\"].mean()\n",
        "df[\"num_of_delays_late_aircraft\"] = df[\"num_of_delays_late_aircraft\"].fillna(late_aircraft_mean)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Calculate total weather delays (30% of late-aircraft delays)\n",
        "df[\"total_weather_delays_B\"] = df[\"num_of_delays_late_aircraft\"] * 0.3\n",
        "\n",
        "# Visualization\n",
        "display(df[[\"airport_code\", \"month\", \"num_of_delays_late_aircraft\", \"total_weather_delays_B\"]].head())"
      ],
      "id": "26ef0897",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Include and execute your code here\n",
        "# Part C: NAS weather delays, with varying percentages by month\n",
        "\n",
        "# Convert to float\n",
        "df[\"num_of_delays_nas\"] = df[\"num_of_delays_nas\"].astype(float)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Function to apply the factor depending on the month\n",
        "def nas_weather(row):\n",
        "    if row[\"month\"] in [\"April\", \"May\", \"June\", \"July\", \"August\"]:\n",
        "        return row[\"num_of_delays_nas\"] * 0.4\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        return row[\"num_of_delays_nas\"] * 0.65\n",
        "\n",
        "# Apply function\n",
        "df[\"total_weather_delays_C\"] = df.apply(nas_weather, axis=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Visualization\n",
        "display(df[[\"airport_code\", \"month\", \"num_of_delays_nas\", \"total_weather_delays_C\"]].head())"
      ],
      "id": "f87ae900",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## QUESTION|TASK 5\n",
        "\n",
        "__Using the new weather variable calculated above, create a barplot showing the proportion of all flights that are delayed by weather at each airport. Describe what you learn from this graph.__  \n",
        "\n",
        "_type your results and analysis here_"
      ],
      "id": "fa50e1de"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## STRETCH QUESTION|TASK 1\n",
        "\n",
        "__Which delay is the worst delay?__ Create a similar analysis as above for Weahter Delay with: Carrier Delay and Security Delay. Compare the proportion of delay for each of the three categories in a Chart and a Table. Describe your results.\n",
        "\n",
        "_type your results and analysis here_\n"
      ],
      "id": "4773e2a6"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Include and execute your code here\n",
        "#| label: Q6\n",
        "#| code-summary: grouped bar chart\n",
        "#| tbl-cap: \"Grouped bar chart of delay proportions\"\n",
        "#| tbl-cap-location: top\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# Replace missing values in carrier delays and convert to integer\n",
        "df[\"num_of_delays_carrier\"] = df[\"num_of_delays_carrier\"].replace(\"NaN\", np.nan).astype(float)\n",
        "df[\"num_of_delays_carrier\"] = df[\"num_of_delays_carrier\"].fillna(df[\"num_of_delays_carrier\"].mean()).astype(int)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Select relevant columns for analysis\n",
        "df_6 = df[[\n",
        "    \"airport_code\", \n",
        "    \"total_weather_delays\", \n",
        "    \"num_of_delays_carrier\", \n",
        "    \"num_of_delays_security\", \n",
        "    \"num_of_flights_total\"\n",
        "]].replace(\"NaN\", np.nan)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Group by airport and calculate the sum for each category\n",
        "table = df_6.groupby(\"airport_code\").agg(\n",
        "    delayed_weather=(\"total_weather_delays\", \"sum\"),\n",
        "    delayed_carrier=(\"num_of_delays_carrier\", \"sum\"),\n",
        "    delayed_security=(\"num_of_delays_security\", \"sum\"),\n",
        "    total_flights=(\"num_of_flights_total\", \"sum\")\n",
        ").reset_index()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Calculate proportion of weather delays\n",
        "weather = table[[\"airport_code\"]].copy()\n",
        "weather[\"proportion\"] = table[\"delayed_weather\"] / table[\"total_flights\"]\n",
        "weather[\"category\"] = \"weather\"\n",
        "\n",
        "# Calculate proportion of carrier delays\n",
        "carrier = table[[\"airport_code\"]].copy()\n",
        "carrier[\"proportion\"] = table[\"delayed_carrier\"] / table[\"total_flights\"]\n",
        "carrier[\"category\"] = \"carrier\"\n",
        "\n",
        "# Calculate proportion of security delays\n",
        "security = table[[\"airport_code\"]].copy()\n",
        "security[\"proportion\"] = table[\"delayed_security\"] / table[\"total_flights\"]\n",
        "security[\"category\"] = \"security\"\n",
        "\n",
        "# Combine all three categories into one DataFrame\n",
        "combined = pd.concat([weather, carrier, security])\n",
        "\n",
        "# Create a grouped bar chart\n",
        "ggplot(data=combined) + \\\n",
        "    geom_bar(\n",
        "        mapping=aes(x='airport_code', y='proportion', fill='category'),\n",
        "        stat='identity',\n",
        "        position='dodge'\n",
        "    ) + \\\n",
        "    labs(\n",
        "        x='Airport Code',\n",
        "        y='Proportion of Delays',\n",
        "        title='Proportion of Delay Types by Airport'\n",
        "    )\n"
      ],
      "id": "f00250aa",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n"
      ],
      "id": "cb23baff"
    }
